cvcpkg: initialize Triangulate's error code before ScalePaths ORs into it.

Clipper2 2.0.1's Triangulate(const PathsD&, int, PathsD&, bool) declares
`int ec;` and passes it to ScalePaths, which does `error_code |= range_error_i`:
a read of an uninitialized int. Every other ScalePaths caller starts from
`int error_code = 0;`. GCC 11 reports this one as -Wmaybe-uninitialized, and
Clipper2 builds its library with -Werror, so it fails to build with GCC (found
by cvcpkg's linux builder; MSVC, clang and emscripten don't flag it). Not yet
reported upstream.

--- a/CPP/Clipper2Lib/src/clipper.triangulation.cpp
+++ b/CPP/Clipper2Lib/src/clipper.triangulation.cpp
@@ -1202,7 +1202,7 @@ namespace Clipper2Lib

   TriangulateResult Triangulate(const PathsD& pp, int decPlaces, PathsD& solution, bool useDelaunay)
   {
-    int ec;
+    int ec = 0;
     double scale;
     TriangulateResult result;
     if (decPlaces <= 0) scale = 1;
